{
  "name": "Making Your Bedroom Safer: A Step-by-Step Guide",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Making your bedroom a safer space can seem like a big job, but breaking it down into simple steps helps a lot. First off, tackle those walking paths! Remove any obstacles, loose rugs, or furniture that you're constantly bumping into. A clear path from your bed to the door and bathroom is crucial. Next, focus on lighting. Think about adding motion-controlled lights or ensuring your lamps are easy to reach from bed. Having a phone or emergency contact list right by your bedside is also a smart move. Then, look at your bed setup. Is it at a comfortable height for getting in and out? Sometimes, small adjustments like bed risers or even grab bars can make a huge difference. Lastly, consider any assistive items you might need. An occupational therapist can be super helpful in figuring out what works best for your unique situation. For more complex changes like wiring or mounting fixtures, it’s best to call in a professional to make sure everything's installed correctly and safely. A little planning goes a long way in creating a secure and comfortable bedroom.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
